# Keyboard commands use the same scoped handler/context machinery as controls.
import key_handling.dl
import focus.dl
import view_lookup.dl
import interaction.dl

to get [the UI event for key] {integer:key} [with modifiers] {integer:modifiers}:
    require condition (0 <= key < 512) reporting "A UI key binding requires a valid key"
    require condition (0 <= modifiers < 16) reporting "UI key modifiers use Shift, Control, Alt and Super bits"
    return 1024 + modifiers * 512 + key

to [bind UI key] {integer:key} [with modifiers] {integer:modifiers} [from] {UI reference:scope} [in] {a pointer to UI instance:instance} [to] {a callback:action} [with context] {a pointer:context}:
    bind scope in instance to action for event (the UI event for key key with modifiers modifiers) with context context

to [unbind UI key] {integer:key} [with modifiers] {integer:modifiers} [from] {UI reference:scope} [in] {a pointer to UI instance:instance}:
    unbind UI handler for scope in instance for event (the UI event for key key with modifiers modifiers)

to [activate a UI key target in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set target to view's instance's event context as UI reference
    set layout to the UI layout for element target in view
    require condition (layout != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI layout)) reporting "The keyboard action targets a control outside its view"
    activate UI layout layout in view

to [bind UI key] {integer:key} [with modifiers] {integer:modifiers} [from] {UI reference:scope} [in] {a pointer to UI instance:instance} [activating] {UI reference:target}:
    bind UI key key with modifiers modifiers from scope in instance to (the function named "activate a UI key target in $") with context (target as a pointer)

to get [process UI key bindings in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    if ((view's input kind != 3) and (view's input kind != 9)) or (view's key press < 0):
        return false
    if (view's active = false) or (view's selection's composing):
        return false
    refresh UI focus in view
    set event to the UI event for key (view's key press) with modifiers (view's modifiers bitwise and 15)
    set layout to view's focused
    if layout = @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI layout):
        set layout to view's layout
    set origin to layout's node
    loop while true:
        if the UI element (layout's node) is enabled in (view's instance):
            set handler to the UI handler for (layout's node) in (view's instance) for event event
            if handler != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI handler):
                invoke UI handler handler for origin in (view's instance) receiving view
                return true
        if layout = view's layout:
            return false
        set layout to the UI parent of layout in view

section when the {C string:label} control receives key {integer:key} with modifiers {integer:modifiers}:
    receiver: a pointer to UI view
    returns: nothing
    value:
        bind UI key key with modifiers modifiers from (the control labeled label in this window) in this window to @intrinsic("deferred body") with context (0 as a pointer)
